config BR2_PACKAGE_EMBRA_INTEL_MICROCODE
	bool "embra-intel-microcode"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_INTEL_MICROCODE
	help
	  Intel's processor microcode at the release embraOS pins: the
	  version in embra-intel-microcode.mk, the archive's sha256 in
	  the hash file beside it. The recipe leaves the files in the
	  images directory, where post_build.sh packs them into
	  /boot/ucode.cpio for the kernel's early loader, and installs
	  Intel's licence under /usr/share/licenses/intel-microcode.

	  Takes the place of Buildroot's intel-microcode package, whose
	  recipe names one release per Buildroot version; the two write
	  the same images directory, so only one is selected.

	  https://github.com/intel/Intel-Linux-Processor-Microcode-Data-Files
